From bca8af76dbe15829825ab008b8afd8166323f8c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ththeod <2376818+ththeod@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:17:25 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 131/138] Balanced PP decode microbatches
 (VLLM_E2_PP_DECODE_BALANCE)

V2 runner + PP + async scheduling: a request decodes every pp_size steps
(next_decode_eligible_step), so the decoding requests form pp_size
microbatches that keep the split admission gave them (6/2 and 7/1 with 8
requests in W37/W38 profiles). Each step's chain through both stages is
paced by the biggest microbatch. With the switch on, a step schedules at
most ceil(decoding / pp_size) decodes; a request over the cap is eligible
again next step, which evens the split out within one cycle.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
